\pard\sa100\sl278\slmult0\cf2\b\fs18 CORE GAME SYSTEMS\cf1\b0\fs21\par

\pard\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f1\fs48 Readable rules, meaningful choices\b0\f0\fs21\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0 The game is built around a small number of systems that interact clearly. The battlefield should remain understandable even when every character model and animation is replaced by a simple coloured capsule.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 The arena and grid\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Battles take place on a flat square-cell grid with no elevation or terrain advantages. Arena silhouettes\f3\emdash such as a tapered rectangle, octagon or grid-approximated circle\emdash are produced by disabling cells outside the playable shape. Every competitive arena is symmetrical and presents identical geometry to both players.\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-230\li490\sa60\sl269\slmult0\tx360\f0 Active cells determine movement, targeting, deployment and line boundaries.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Inactive cells are treated as nonexistent, not as blocked terrain.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}The visual colosseum can change theme without changing the fair gameplay layout.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 Units and fantasy races\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Each race begins with three accessible roles: a durable tank or frontliner, a ranged unit and an inexpensive pawn-style unit. Levelling that race unlocks a broader roster without making the starters irrelevant.\par
Shared archetypes\f3\emdash Warriors, Archers and Mages\emdash make the game easy to learn. Race-specific classes supply identity: Humans may field Paladins, Undead may use Necromancers, and Orcs may rely on Shamans. Mature races can culminate in one or two signature classes, while ideas such as Vampires, Werewolves and Witchcraft can become advanced branches or complete rosters.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 Point-buy army construction\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Players do not take every unlocked unit into battle. They construct a team under two limits:\par

\pard{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf5\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\fi-230\li490\sa60\sl269\slmult0\tx360 Points control the overall value and power of the army.\par
{\pntext\f5\'B7\tab}Capacity limits the number or battlefield weight of units that can be fielded.\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0 This creates meaningful trade-offs between a small elite force, a larger group of basic units or a specialised formation built around a particular strategy.\par
\page\par

\pard\sa100\sl278\slmult0\cf2\b\fs18 CORE GAME SYSTEMS \f3\emdash  CONTINUED\cf1\b0\fs21\par

\pard\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f1\fs48 Deployment, direction and tempo\b0\f0\fs21\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0 The battle begins before the first attack. Formation, facing and the delay between activations are intended to make each commitment visible, predictable and open to counterplay.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 Hidden deployment and simultaneous reveal\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Before combat, each player arranges their army privately on the three-row formation area shown from their own perspective. Ready locks the formation. Once both players are ready, the complete armies are placed onto the arena together and the board is revealed. Neither player gains an advantage by reacting to the opponent\rquote s visible placement.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 Movement, facing and attacks\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Units are defined by reusable movement and attack patterns. One might advance directly, another move diagonally, and another leap over occupied cells. Facing gives directional attacks and defensive positioning real meaning. Selecting a unit shows its legal movement cells and attack area before the player commits.\par

\pard\keep\keepn\sb300\sa140\sl278\slmult0\b\f2\fs32 Turn and recovery system\par

\pard\sa120\sl278\slmult0\b0\f0\fs21 Players alternate activating one ready unit. A unit can move, choose its facing, attack or wait, then receives a recovery counter based on the action and unit. Recovery counts down on later turns; only units at zero can act. Powerful units therefore hit harder but may leave longer openings, while lighter units influence the battle more frequently.\par
